---
layout: base.njk
title: Events
---
{% import "macros.njk" as m with context %}
{% set upcoming = events.events | upcoming(build.today) %}
<h1>Events</h1>
<p>The chapter runs events for Rensselaer students throughout the year.</p>
<p><strong>Chapter meetings.</strong> {{ chapter.meeting.when }}, in {{ chapter.meeting.where }}. Meetings are open to everyone.</p>
{{ m.stale(chapter.meeting.verified) }}

<h2>Upcoming events</h2>
{% for e in upcoming %}{{ m.event(e, true) }}{% endfor %}
<p class="tba-block"{% if upcoming.length %} {{ m.showAfter((upcoming | last).date) }}{% endif %}>No upcoming events posted yet. Announcements go out on the chapter's social accounts, linked in the footer.</p>

<h2>The I/O talk series</h2>
<p>An I/O is a talk that introduces students to a useful technology they might not meet in class. A speaker who knows the topic explains what it is, what problems it solves, and how to use it. Each talk also appears in the archive below with its description.</p>
<ul class="award-list">
  {% for e in events.events | selectattr("kind") %}<li><span class="award-year">{{ e.date | monthYear }}</span> {{ e.title }}</li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>

<h2>Past events</h2>
{% for year, items in events.events | pastByYear(build.today) %}
<details{% if loop.first %} open{% endif %}>
  <summary>{{ year }} ({{ items.length }} event{% if items.length != 1 %}s{% endif %})</summary>
  {% for e in items %}{{ m.event(e) }}{% endfor %}
</details>
{% endfor %}
